  "_doc": "Per-language WORDS for write_claim_guard.py: how a reply CLAIMS it saved something (a list item, a calendar event, a reminder, a note, a timer). Data, not code: a new language or phrasing is a new row here, never a new regex. A claim verb counts in the active (I've added) and the completed passive (passive_done: has been added; passive_past: was added, which also needs a target noun unless the verb is added); a present-tense passive (passive_state: is scheduled for Friday) describes the calendar and is a claim only for a verb marked state_claim (is added). Every word is matched after NFKC + casefold + diacritic stripping (so 'anadi' == 'añadí'), against whole tokens. 'reviewed' = read by a native speaker; en is, es is not yet (E6 in docs/research/structural-floors-2026-10-09.md). clause_temporals (after, when, once, before): a TRAILING one opens a clause of its own, so a completed claim before it still counts (I have added milk, after you asked me to); a LEADING one blocks its own clause; a present-tense passive before one (is added once you tap Done) stays a description. IN-PROGRESS claims (a claim verb with form 'progressive' - Adding X to your list now, I'm setting a reminder - or a promise_verbs base form, which counts ONLY after a promise_subjects word (I'll, I will: the promise_blockers 'will' then blocks only the other claim forms) AND with an immediacy word in its clause - I'll add that to your list right now) say the write is happening in THIS turn (a bare sentence-opening progressive needs one of implied_cues - now, for you - or a first-person subject: 'Adding milk to your list by tapping +' is an instruction): they are judged at the END of the turn (the brain may narrate just before its tool call), and blocked only if no receipt landed by then. STANDING PROMISES (standing_promises: a promise subject + a promise verb with NO immediacy word - 'I'll remind you to call the plumber at 2:30', 'I'll add milk to your list') are in-progress claims too, unless the unit holds a promise_deferrals word (later, as soon as) or an 'if', opens with a temporal clause (After I've added milk, I'll set a reminder), or the promise's clause is followed by a temporal one (once you confirm), or the user's own turn opens with one of standing_skip_openers ('what reminders have I got?': a future-tense reply then DESCRIBES). An untargeted 'I'll add it' (needs_target), 'Shall I add it?' and 'I can add it if you like' stay offers, never claims. REMOVALS (claim / promise verbs with action 'remove': removed, taken ... off, I'll cancel) claim the REMOVAL kind of their target (removal_kinds: list -> list_removed; a note or a memory -> forget); 'particles' are words that must follow the verb in its clause (taken OFF, forgotten THAT). claim_phrases are whole-phrase claims (got that noted, consider it forgotten) with their kind. honest_by_kind replaces the honest line for a claim whose first kind is listed. correction_note / correction_kinds / history_marker are what ZOE_WRITE_CLAIM_CORRECTION hands the brain after a blocked claim (claim_correction.py). An ASSURANCE - a promise verb after assurance_subjects (I can) with one of assurance_words (certainly, absolutely) in its unit - is an in-progress claim only in a turn whose write was deferred to the brain or with an immediacy word: 'I can certainly set that reminder for you' (QA 2026-11-05: said, then the tool failed). In a turn whose write the fast path DEFERRED to the brain, an in-progress claim with no target noun ('Adding those now.') claims the deferred kind, but only with one of implied_cues in its clause ('Adding salt makes it better' is no claim). promise_fillers are words a promise subject may stand behind before its verb (I'll MAKE SURE I remember); a promise subject of up to three words (I'm going to) counts like I'll, and its 'going' / 'gonna' then block only the other claim forms (promise_blockers). ON AN EMOTIONAL TURN (memory_gate.is_emotional_turn - the user's own words carry feeling, lexicons_data/emotional_cues.json) a blocked claim of only memory / note kinds is DROPPED, never replaced: the honest line would land in the middle of a disclosure. The brain is still told (correction_note); emotional_quiet is said only when nothing else of the reply is left.",
